jobDescription:
&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Airbnb was born in 2007 when two hosts welcomed three guests to their San Francisco home, and has since grown to over 5 million hosts who have welcomed over 2 billion guest arrivals in almost every country across the globe. Every day, hosts offer unique stays and experiences that make it possible for guests to connect with communities in a more authentic way.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Community You Will Join:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Airbnb is seeking an Accounting Intern to join the Statutory Reporting team for our Summer Intern Program.&lt;br&gt;If hired, you’ll have the opportunity to work with the Statutory Reporting team, as well as work with multiple cross-functional partners such as GL accounting, tax, and legal. &amp;nbsp;The Statutory Reporting team works with these cross-functional teams to prepare financial statements for Airbnb entities outside of the United States. &amp;nbsp;This team also works with auditors to ensure that Airbnb’s financial information being reported are accurate, complete, and follows all the rules and regulations in different countries. &amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Difference You Will Make:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;You&#39;ll play an important part in ensuring Airbnb’s financial reporting outside the US is accurate and compliant. This includes analyzing accounts and identifying adjustments needed so statutory books meet local requirements. You’ll get hands-on experience drafting financial statements, and you’ll support auditors by organizing and providing key documents. You’ll also build your project management skills as you help keep audits on track and meet deadlines.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A Typical Day:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As an intern, you’ll be integrated into the Statutory Reporting team where you’ll contribute to impactful projects. Your manager, team, and our incredible employee community will strive to be superhosts to you during the summer. We provide the support, mentorship, fun, and real world experience needed to accelerate your learning. You can expect to:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Be an audit detective&lt;/strong&gt;: support multiple statutory audits by gathering key supporting documents (bank statements, GL listings, invoices, etc.) in response to auditor inquiries.&amp;nbsp; See how organizations ensure compliance and accuracy first-hand!&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Tackle real-world surveys&lt;/strong&gt;: prepare responses to important business surveys and collect the right documentation to back them up&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Analyze and test financial data&lt;/strong&gt;: dive into sampling and testing journal entries, sharpening your analytical skills and data-integrity know-how&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Investigate unrecorded liabilities&lt;/strong&gt;: perform search for unrecorded liabilities - learn to spot what’s missing and why it matters&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Hands-on with financial statements&lt;/strong&gt;: support the preparation of statutory financial statements and experience the full reporting cycle&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Journal entry experience&lt;/strong&gt;: post statutory journal entries, gaining practical experience with accounting systems and controls&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your Expertise:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This opportunity is for &lt;strong&gt;first-year, Masters in Accounting students (preferred) and Masters in Finance students &lt;/strong&gt;with the following background:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are a full-time student graduating between December 2026 - Spring 2027&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficient in Microsoft Excel and Google Sheets, including advanced knowledge of formulas, pivot tables, and data analysis tools&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communication and analytical skills, with the ability to clearly articulate thoughts, insights, and problem-solving approaches&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong attention to detail with a focus on accuracy and precision in work&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong organizational skills and excellent time management, with the ability to manage multiple projects and tasks simultaneously&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Passion for the Airbnb mission and product; experience with the platform is a plus!&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work authorization for employment in the United States is required (CPT/OPT is accepted) - visa sponsorship and relocation to the US is unavailable&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Preferred but not expected:&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Previous internship experience or full-time experience in accounting or auditing&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with Enterprise Resource Planning (ERP) systems like Oracle and NetSuite (preferred)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your Location:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;This position is US - Remote Eligible. The role may include occasional work at an Airbnb office or attendance at offsites, as agreed to with your manager. While the position is Remote Eligible, you must live in a state where Airbnb, Inc. has a registered entity.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://careers.airbnb.com/&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;a style=&quot;color: #000000;&quot; href=&quot;https://careers.airbnb.com/&quot;&gt;Click here for the up-to-date list of excluded states. This list is continuously evolving, so please check back with us if the state you live in is on the exclusion list&lt;/a&gt; &lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;If your position is employed by another Airbnb entity, your recruiter will inform you what states you are eligible to work from.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;How to apply:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Submit your resume and a cover letter that addresses the questions below:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Which Airbnb Core Value most resonates with you and why?&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;What do you hope to gain from this internship with the Statutory Reporting team?&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Select one of the experiences/projects listed on your resume and expand on why it makes you a strong candidate for this role.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our Commitment to Inclusion &amp;amp; Belonging:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Airbnb is committed to working with the broadest talent pool possible. We believe diverse ideas foster innovation and engagement, and allow us to attract creatively-led people, and to develop the best products, services and solutions. All qualified individuals are encouraged to apply.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We strive to also provide a disability inclusive application and interview process. If you are a candidate with a disability and require reasonable accommodation in order to submit an application, please contact us at: &lt;/span&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;mailto:reasonableaccommodations@airbnb.com&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;reasonableaccommodations@airbnb.com&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;. Please include your full name, the role you’re applying for and the accommodation necessary to assist you with the recruiting process.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We ask that you only reach out to us if you are a candidate whose disability prevents you from being able to complete our online application.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 16px;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;How we’ll take care of you:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400; font-size: 16px;&quot;&gt;Our job titles may span more than one career or degree level. This role may also be eligible for benefits and Employee Travel Credits.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Pay Range&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$28&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$32 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Airbnb was born in 2007 when two hosts welcomed three guests to their San Francisco home, and has since grown to over 5 million hosts who have welcomed over 2 billion guest arrivals in almost every country across the globe. Every day, hosts offer unique stays and experiences that make it possible for guests to connect with communities in a more authentic way.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Community You Will Join&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Join our dynamic Research Team, which provides Airbnb with actionable insights to inform strategic decisions. You’ll be part of Innovation Insights, a division of Research that delivers insight into cultural trends, the competitive landscape, key audience segments, and new growth opportunities to help shape the future of Airbnb. Innovation Insights is also at the forefront of accelerating research and delivering critical insights using custom-built, cutting-edge AI tools and methods.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Difference You Will Make&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As AI-Enabled Insights Lead, you will develop and run AI-powered analyses to uncover actionable insight into travelers and travel trends globally, current and prospective Airbnb guests, and current and prospective Airbnb hosts. You will partner with stakeholders across the Research, Strategy, Product, Engineering, Data Science, Analytics and Marketing teams. Your work will grow our competitive advantage via trailblazing, AI-driven research and insights that fuel Airbnb innovation.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A Typical Day&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with a best-in-class research team to deliver insights that impact business strategies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with internal and cross-functional partners to identify opportunities to drive research efficiencies and business impact.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead and collaborate on building innovative AI-powered methods, including leveraging third-party and in-house tools/infrastructure to build AI-orchestrated pipelines customized for insights-driven analyses.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analyze large scale structured and unstructured data from internal sources (e.g., guest searches and reviews), primary research (e.g., interviews conducted globally at scale), and external sources (e.g., social media or chatbot conversations).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Combine NLP with advanced data analysis and statistical modeling to uncover relationships, test hypotheses and extract new insights.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Augment the team’s already advanced use of AI as a complement to, and catalyst for, human insights and expertise.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage the team’s program for identifying third-party AI tools that add value and extend our capabilities.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Learn from, and share with, the Airbnb technical community.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your Expertise&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advanced degree in a quantitative human-oriented field preferred (social science, cognitive science, psychology, neuroscience, economics, etc.) and 5+ years industry experience.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Expertise in using Python, SQL and agentic coding tools such as Claude Code, Codex, and/or Cursor.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track record of success in leveraging NLP for the purpose of uncovering insights into human motivations and behaviors.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Technical expertise in cutting-edge AI techniques and building AI-orchestrated pipelines to analyze complex data.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;History of strong communication and collaboration with cross-functional partners, including partners with and without technical backgrounds.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated willingness to continue learning, adopt technologies/approaches, and collaborate and share with the technical community.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to balance a detail-oriented, hands-on approach with creative, “outside-the-box” thinking.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Growth-minded, solutions-oriented approach with a history of driving projects from idea to impact.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 16px;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);&quot;&gt;How We&#39;ll Take Care of You:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;p1&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 16px;&quot;&gt;Our job titles may span more than one career level. The actual base pay is dependent upon many factors, such as: training, transferable skills, work experience, business needs and market demands. The base pay range is subject to change and may be modified in the future. This role may also be eligible for bonus, equity, benefits, and Employee Travel Credits. &amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Pay Range&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$176,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$220,000 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Airbnb was born in 2007 when two hosts welcomed three guests to their San Francisco home, and has since grown to over 5 million hosts who have welcomed over 2 billion guest arrivals in almost every country across the globe. Every day, hosts offer unique stays and experiences that make it possible for guests to connect with communities in a more authentic way.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The community you will join:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Airbnb is seeking Communications Interns for our 2026 Summer Intern Program.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Communications team is responsible for telling the Airbnb story around the world. Whether it&#39;s speaking to media and bloggers, Hosts and guests, industry commentators, thought leaders or the wider community, the Communications team is the voice of Airbnb. As an intern, you’ll be matched to one of the following sub-teams:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Trust Communications/Media Relations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Channel Communication&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;text-align: left;&quot;&gt;Consumer Communication&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Communication Operations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Internal Communication&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The difference you will make:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As an intern, you’ll be integrated into a team where you’ll contribute to challenging projects. Your manager, team, and our incredible employee community will strive to be superhosts to you during the summer. We provide the support, mentorship, fun, and real world experience needed to accelerate your learning and make a real impact on our product, as Airbnb revolutionizes connection, belonging, and travel. You can expect to:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own and complete a capstone project from beginning to end&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with multiple team members to achieve project milestones&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Communicate with stakeholders across different teams to provide project updates&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Seek and provide feedback throughout the internship&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Actively participate in and contribute to the Communications team and broader Airbnb community&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A typical day:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll get first-hand experience on what it is like to be on the Communications team at Airbnb. You can expect to:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor and analyze brand and competitor social media, providing insights and research&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analyze social media performance for brand and influencer partners, preparing metrics and reports&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create slide decks, documents, and compile editorial press pitches and Newsroom posts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Facilitate Host outreach for approvals on featuring stays in press and obtaining photo credits&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support program management of campaigns, including drafting briefs, press materials, and maintaining trackers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assist in talent consultant needs, team coordination, and scheduling meetings/travel&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with internal teams and agencies to develop global media strategies for consumer campaigns&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stay informed about evolving trends through social media monitoring and news cycles, identifying press opportunities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track performance of evergreen influencer program&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage inbound influencer requests&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Flag and contribute to opportunities for real-time social content&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help plan surprise &amp;amp; delight trips based on social media listening&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Important Note: &lt;/em&gt;The Communications team is global and frequently works with employees in other time zones. If hired as an intern, you may need to accommodate global teammates from time-to-time, but should expect to primarily be available during Pacific Time business hours.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your expertise:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This opportunity is for &lt;strong&gt;third-year Bachelor students&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;strong&gt;graduating between December 2026 - June 2027 &lt;/strong&gt;with the following skills and background:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Undergraduate major or graduate program in Communications, Journalism, Media Studies, Public Relations, or similar field&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Previously worked in a PR agency, Communications team, or newsroom&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent writing skills with a keen eye for detail to ensure accuracy and quality&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong verbal communication abilities complemented by interpersonal skills that allows effective collaboration&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficient in time management and organization, with the ability to manage quick and unexpected deadlines&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Adaptability and flexibility to handle fast-paced environments and unexpected deadlines&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with social media platforms and landscapes (ie. X, TikTok, LinkedIn, etc.)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in building organic campaigns and strategies for favorable press and social buzz, creating social media content, or community engagement&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Interest in and basic understanding of the business and branding and a passion for pop culture, social media, and trends&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Passion for the Airbnb mission; experience with the platform is a plus!&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work authorization for employment in the United States is required - visa sponsorship is unavailable&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your location:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This position is US - Remote Eligible. The role may include occasional work at an Airbnb office or attendance at offsites, as agreed to with your manager. While the position is Remote Eligible, you must live in a state where Airbnb, Inc. has a registered entity. &lt;a href=&quot;https://careers.airbnb.com/&quot;&gt;Click here&lt;/a&gt; for the up-to-date list of excluded states. This list is continuously evolving, so please check back with us if the state you live in is on the exclusion list. If your position is employed by another Airbnb entity, your recruiter will inform you what states you are eligible to work from.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our commitment to inclusion &amp;amp; belonging:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Airbnb is committed to working with the broadest talent pool possible. We believe diverse ideas foster innovation and engagement, and allow us to attract creatively-led people, and to develop the best products, services and solutions. All qualified individuals are encouraged to apply.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We strive to also provide a disability inclusive application and interview process. If you are a candidate with a disability and require reasonable accommodation in order to submit an application, please contact us at: reasonableaccommodations@airbnb.com. Please include your full name, the role you’re applying for and the accommodation necessary to assist you with the recruiting process.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We ask that you only reach out to us if you are a candidate whose disability prevents you from being able to complete our online application.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;How we’ll take care of you:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our job titles may span more than one career or degree level. This role may also be eligible for benefits and Employee Travel Credits.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Currency:&lt;/strong&gt; USD&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &lt;strong&gt;Pay rate: &lt;/strong&gt;$28 per hour&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;How to apply:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In addition to your resume, please submit:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A cover letter that answers the following questions:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;What is your favorite Airbnb media campaign to date and why?&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;What are your near-term or long-term career goals and how will this internship with the Airbnb Communications team help you get there?&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Select one of the experiences/projects listed on your resume and expand on why it makes you a strong candidate for the Communications Intern role.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A writing sample or portfolio that showcases your communication skills.&lt;/strong&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;This can be an assignment from a Communications or related course, a blog post, news article, op-ed, social media copy, or similar piece of writing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;We ask that you submit a writing sample that you have already created (e.g., a class assignment, published work, or personal project). There is no need to write something new specifically for this application.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The writing sample should be 2–3 pages of content. If submitting a shorter piece, such as social media copy, please combine multiple examples to meet this length requirement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Airbnb was born in 2007 when two hosts welcomed three guests to their San Francisco home, and has since grown to over 5 million hosts who have welcomed over 2 billion guest arrivals in almost every country across the globe. Every day, hosts offer unique stays and experiences that make it possible for guests to connect with communities in a more authentic way.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; color: #000000;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Community You Will Join:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; color: #000000;&quot;&gt;The Airbnb Hotels team is a fun, fast-growing group leading Airbnb’s expansion into the hotel sector. Operating with an entrepreneurial spirit, this team combines the simplicity, product excellence, and guest-centered ethos that define Airbnb. This team’s mission is to deliver the smoothest, most intuitive hotel booking experience for guests, while helping hotels easily drive incremental bookings so they can focus on delivering the best hospitality. The ultimate aim is to help more people discover high-quality hotels, creating value for guests and our hotel partners.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; color: #000000;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Difference You Will Make:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; color: #000000;&quot;&gt;In this role, you will provide specialist API support and act as a subject matter expert for our connectivity operations. Your responsibilities include conducting analysis and technical troubleshooting to solve complex problems, monitoring key metrics, and error logs to optimize performance or for&amp;nbsp; ensuring timely error resolution. You&#39;ll serve as a technical point of contact for both internal and external partners, offering expert insight into Airbnb’s api’s and our partner systems. You’ll support the Connectivity Team and Enterprise Account Team&amp;nbsp; with projects designed to achieve Airbnb’s commercial goals. You&#39;ll also help to create and improve internal knowledge bases and training materials so teams can independently handle API-related questions.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; color: #000000;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A Typical Day:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use data to identify strategic opportunities and drive sales growth&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide day-to-day technical support for internal and external systems, including connectivity issues, to proactively mitigate partner impact&lt;/li&gt;
