&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll be doing:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own and drive Coinbase’s overall business performance in Canada, with accountability for user growth, revenue, and long-term market position&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define and execute the country strategy, identifying high-impact growth opportunities grounded in market, regulatory, and competitive analysis&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Product, Engineering, and Design to shape and launch locally-relevant products, ensuring strong product-market fit within regulatory constraints&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead cross-functional execution in partnership with Marketing, Business Development, Legal, Compliance, and Policy to deliver Canada-specific initiatives at speed&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Play a senior leadership role in regulatory and policy engagement, helping unlock new products and ensure ongoing compliance with Canadian requirements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build, hire, and develop a high-performing local team, while reinforcing Coinbase’s mission, values, and operating standards&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as a senior representative of Coinbase in Canada, engaging with regulators, key partners, clients, media, and industry forums as appropriate&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as a connective tissue between Canada and global teams, ensuring alignment with global priorities while advocating for local needs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Communicate clearly and credibly with executives and cross-functional leaders, synthesizing complex issues into actionable insights and decisions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What we look for in you:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Senior leadership experience (CEO, COO, GM, Founder, or equivalent) leading and scaling a fintech business in Canada, with measurable impact on revenue and/or active users&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Completion of the Canadian Securities Institute (CSI) – Partners, Directors and Senior Officers Course (PDO) and a minimum of 5 years’ experience in the financial services industry&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep understanding of the Canadian regulated financial services ecosystem, including experience operating under regulatory oversight&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven track record partnering with Product, Marketing, and Business Development to build, launch, and scale products in regulated environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Direct experience engaging with regulators and policy stakeholders, with the ability to balance constructive relationships and commercial outcomes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of how regulated financial institutions operate across functions such as Compliance, Risk, Finance, Treasury, Audit, and third-party oversight&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable operating in a remote-first, globally matrixed organization, aligning local execution with global standards&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Highly pragmatic and solutions-oriented, with a bias toward action and continuous improvement&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional written and verbal communication skills in English, with the ability to influence senior stakeholders and external audiences&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Structured, analytical problem-solver who can navigate ambiguity and make sound decisions with imperfect information&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong interest in crypto and blockchain (prior expertise helpful but not required), with curiosity and conviction about the space’s future&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Nice to haves:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Previous experience working in a multinational / US-headquartered business&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with retail-oriented payments, trading, or brokerage platforms&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Previous work experience or personal interest in crypto/blockchain space&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
