&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Team/ Role:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Sitting within Platform PG, the Identity Verification (IDV) team operates Coinbase&#39;s centralized identity verification platform, delivering the most trusted forms of customer identity verification in a secure, scalable, and developer-friendly way. IDV is critical to Coinbase&#39;s compliance posture (KYC/AML) and security posture (ensuring the person accessing an account is the legitimate account holder). This role will own the end-to-end IDV platform, including vendor integrations, document capture SDKs, decisioning logic, fraud detection, and the platformization roadmap that enables seamless adoption by any Coinbase product.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll be doing (ie. job duties):&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the end-to-end Identity Verification platform strategy, roadmap, and execution&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive platformization efforts to enable CUJ owners to configure IDV requirements, decision rules, and vendor preferences self-serve&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage vendor relationships and optimize routing across IDV vendors (Onfido, Au10tix, Persona, etc.) to maximize success rates, minimize fraud, and optimize costs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead initiatives to combat synthetic fraud and AI-generated identity attacks through new detection features, challenges, and e-ID integrations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deliver composable IDV components (document collection, liveness, facematch, motion) that can operate independently for various CUJs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner closely with Engineering, Design, Risk, Compliance, and CX to deliver world-class IDV experiences&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define and track key metrics including IDV success rates, fraud rates, P90 processing time, and contact rates&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and ship developer-friendly APIs, SDKs, testbench tooling, and observability to accelerate product team integrations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What we look for in you (ie. job requirements):&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;7+ years of product management experience, with significant experience in Identity, Verification, Trust &amp;amp; Safety, or adjacent domains&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building and scaling platform products with self-serve configuration, APIs, and SDKs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong technical aptitude with the ability to partner effectively with engineering on complex backend systems and vendor integrations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with vendor management, including performance evaluation, contract negotiation, and multi-vendor routing optimization&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to balance competing priorities across fraud prevention, user experience, and cost optimization&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical skills with experience defining and tracking success metrics&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent written and verbal communication skills; ability to influence cross-functional stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working in a regulated environment (fintech, payments, or similar)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Nice to haves:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with document verification, biometrics, liveness detection, or e-ID technologies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with ML-powered fraud detection or synthetic identity detection&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Crypto, blockchain, or fintech experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with international market expansion and geo-specific compliance requirements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
