&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Ready to be pushed beyond what you think you’re capable of?&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Coinbase, our mission is to increase economic freedom in the world. It’s a massive, ambitious opportunity that demands the best of us, every day, as we build the emerging onchain platform — and with it, the future global financial system.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;To achieve our mission, we’re seeking a very specific candidate. We want someone who is passionate about our mission and who believes in the power of crypto and blockchain technology to update the financial system. We want someone who is eager to leave their mark on the world, who relishes the pressure and privilege of working with high caliber colleagues, and who actively seeks feedback to keep leveling up. We want someone who will run towards, not away from, solving the company’s hardest problems.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.coinbase.com/mission&quot;&gt;work culture&lt;/a&gt; is intense and isn’t for everyone. But if you want to build the future alongside others who excel in their disciplines and expect the same from you, there’s no better place to be.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;While many roles at Coinbase are remote-first, we are not remote-only. In-person participation is required throughout the year. Team and company-wide offsites are held multiple times annually to foster collaboration, connection, and alignment. Attendance is expected and fully supported.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;The Employee &amp;amp; Workplace Experience (EWX) team owns the places and programs that shape how Coinbase employees connect, collaborate, and come together. As a remote-first company, EWX ensures that in-person time is intentional, well run, and operating clearly, consistently, and at scale. This role sits at the center of EWX operations, focusing on building the structure and operating systems that enable others to execute well.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll be doing (ie. job duties):&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Run the Rhythm of the Business -&amp;nbsp;Own planning cycles, weekly prioritization, launch readiness, and retrospectives for EWX.Translate leadership direction into clear plans, milestones, and ownership.&lt;br&gt;Surface risks, dependencies, and resourcing issues early.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Support Go-to-Market for EWX Programs -&amp;nbsp;Support the planning and delivery of surges, working sessions, event grants, and office-related initiatives.&amp;nbsp;Coordinate across Workplace, Real Estate, Internal Comms, Finance, and other partners.&amp;nbsp;Build simple intake and prioritization mechanisms to prevent ad hoc work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Budget Management -&amp;nbsp;Track budgets for EWX programs and initiatives.&amp;nbsp;Maintain clear visibility into forecast versus actuals.&amp;nbsp;Flag trade-offs and risks early to help leadership make informed decisions.&lt;br&gt;Partner with Finance on planning and reforecasting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Real Estate and Program Planning Support -&amp;nbsp;Support real estate planning work, including capacity assumptions, utilization inputs, and timing.Track cross-functional inputs and decisions.&amp;nbsp;Ensure assumptions and decisions are documented and communicated clearly.&amp;nbsp;Note: You do not own design or construction, but you help keep planning tight and aligned.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Process, Systems, and Tools -&amp;nbsp;Build and maintain repeatable processes, playbooks, and operating models.&amp;nbsp;Reduce one-off work and ambiguity.&amp;nbsp;Ensure tools like Asana, Jira, Notion, and Sheets support clarity and scale.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Data, Reporting, and Storytelling -&amp;nbsp;Help define what success looks like for EWX programs.&amp;nbsp;Build dashboards and simple reporting to show progress, spend, and impact.&amp;nbsp;Turn updates into clear written summaries for leadership.&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What we look for in you (ie. job requirements):&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Five to seven plus years in operations, program management, business operations, or a similar role.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Strong systems thinker who builds structure to prevent repeated problem-solving.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Comfortable managing budgets and financial trade-offs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Able to operate with ambiguity and translate direction into action.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Clear and concise communicator, especially in writing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Data-literate and comfortable working with metrics and dashboards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Works well with cross-functional partners without needing formal authority.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Nice to haves:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Experience in a remote-first or globally distributed company&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Familiarity with the Google Workspace suite&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Certification or advanced experience with project/program management tools like Asana or Jira&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;PID# : P75847&lt;/p&gt;
