&lt;p&gt;While many roles at Coinbase are remote-first, we are not remote-only. In-person participation is required throughout the year. Team and company-wide offsites are held multiple times annually to foster collaboration, connection, and alignment. Attendance is expected and fully supported.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;Join Coinbase&#39;s Financial Services &amp;amp; Loyalty (FS&amp;amp;L) team to build Trade-Fi utility using blockchain advantages. FS&amp;amp;L is responsible for high-impact products like payments, credit card, on-chain borrowing and lending, staking, and CB One subscription, serving millions of users.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for a deeply technical leader to define the North Star engineering vision for diver FS&amp;amp;L, drive architectural cohesion across our diverse product suite, and ensure our high-throughput systems are scalable and reliable. You will lead multi-quarter, cross-organizational initiatives and be a critical mentor to other senior engineers.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Be Doing&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define and drive the technical vision and strategy for FS&amp;amp;L, ensuring systems achieve high throughput, low latency, and scale.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Architect and build mission-critical financial systems (e.g., card processing, loan repayments) with a focus on funds flow, reconciliation, and invariants.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive developer productivity by advocating for new tooling (Go, Temporal, K8, MongoDB) and AI adoption.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mentor and coach team members to foster growth and technical excellence.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Product/Engineering leaders to align on long-term product and engineering strategy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead the creation of reusable platforms for adoption across Coinbase.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We Look For In You (Must-Haves)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years of software engineering experience in large-scale distributed systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep expertise in payments or traditional finance.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated experience in architecting and building high-throughput, low-latency financial systems that can handle $500M monthly processing volumes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of funds flow, reconciliation, and invariants.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to lead complex, cross-organizational initiatives and drive architectural cohesion.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong mentoring skills and a passion for leveling up teammates.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working on consumer products with a bias towards strong design and UX.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Nice to Haves&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with Go or other performant backend languages.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with vendor integrations (Cardless, Morpho) and regulated environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Crypto-forward experience (e.g., on-chain activity, blockchain payment journeys).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Job ID: P71000&lt;/p&gt;
