&lt;p&gt;As an Associate Event Marketing Manager – Communications on Datadog’s Events team, you’ll play a key role in delivering strategic, on-brand communications that elevate DASH—our flagship annual conference—and our global Datadog Summit series. You&#39;ll help execute multi-channel marketing campaigns that drive registration, engagement, and attendance while reinforcing Datadog’s value across every event touchpoint. This is a high-impact opportunity for a creative, detail-oriented marketer to sharpen their skills in event marketing, communications, and cross-functional program management.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Datadog, we place value in our office culture - the relationships and collaboration it builds and the creativity it brings to the table. We operate as a hybrid workplace to ensure our Datadogs can create a work-life harmony that best fits them.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You’ll Do:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support the end-to-end development of event communications for DASH and Datadog Summits, with a focus on registration growth and attendee engagement&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with creative teams to develop on-brand marketing assets—including banners, social graphics, and promotional videos—for global use&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage campaign execution and communications workflows, partnering with Marketing Operations to ensure timely, high-quality delivery&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate with corporate marketing and demand generation to support organic and paid campaign execution that drives awareness and pipeline&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with regional and localization teams to deliver in-language event communications for global Summits&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create internal enablement materials—talking points, FAQs, messaging—to align GTM teams around event goals and updates&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who You Are:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;1–3+ years of experience in event marketing, field marketing, digital marketing, or corporate communications—ideally in B2B SaaS or a technical environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A strong communicator with a clear, concise writing style and the ability to translate event value to technical audiences across channels&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Organized and detail-oriented, with project management strengths and comfort working within structured workflows, approvals, and SLAs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design-aware and visually attuned—you know how to build clean decks and communicate information clearly and effectively&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Skilled at collaborating cross-functionally and managing feedback from diverse stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiar with event and marketing tools such as Cvent, Airtable, Jira, Confluence, Salesforce, and analytics platforms like Metabase or Tableau&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;This position requires up to 25% travel for business purposes, which may include domestic and/or international travel as needed to fulfill job responsibilities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Datadog values people from all walks of life. We understand not everyone will meet all the above qualifications on day one. That&#39;s okay. If you’re passionate about technology and want to grow your skills, we encourage you to apply.&lt;/p&gt;
