&lt;p&gt;Datadog is seeking a highly organized and execution-focused &lt;strong&gt;Associate Field Marketing Manager&lt;/strong&gt; to support the East NAMER region. This role is ideal for someone who enjoys event logistics, thrives in a fast-paced environment, and is passionate about delivering seamless client-facing experiences.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As part of the NAMER Field Marketing team, you will own the execution and operational delivery of regional programs, including hospitality events, third-party sponsorships, vendor coordination, and scalable initiatives such as event-in-a-box programs for emerging products. This role is critical in supporting pipeline-generating programs while enabling Field Marketing Managers to focus on strategic planning and product-aligned campaigns.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;At Datadog, we value our office culture - the relationships and collaboration it builds and the creativity it brings. We operate as a hybrid workplace to help our Datadogs create work-life harmony that fits them best.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You’ll Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support pipeline driving activities for Mid-market East accounts, ensuring smooth delivery from planning through post-event follow-up&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate hospitality events, executive dinners, third-party sponsorships, regional activations, and local programs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage vendors, contracts, shipping, inventory, on-site logistics, and budget tracking&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support scalable initiatives such as event-in-a-box kits and repeatable regional playbooks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner closely with Sales and Field Marketing Managers to align programs with territory priorities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assist with campaign setup, tracking, and reporting in marketing and sales systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain documentation and help build processes that improve efficiency and repeatability&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support execution of larger Datadog programs including DASH-related initiatives, Summits, Datadog Live, and industry events like re:Invent, Google Cloud Next, RSA&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who You Are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;1–2 years of experience in field marketing, event marketing, event coordination, or program support&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Highly organized with strong attention to detail and time management skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable managing multiple projects and deadlines in a fast-paced environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proactive and dependable, with a strong sense of ownership over execution&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Clear communicator who collaborates well across Sales, Marketing, and cross-functional teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Process-oriented and interested in building scalable ways of working&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with marketing or sales tools (e.g., SFDC, Marketo) is a plus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent verbal and written communication skills, with the ability to present ideas thoughtfully and clearly to influence and collaborate effectively across all levels of the organization&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to travel up to 50% of the time&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Datadog values people from all walks of life. We understand not everyone will meet every qualification on day one — and that’s okay. If you’re excited about technology and eager to grow your career in field marketing, we encourage you to apply.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
