&lt;p style=&quot;color: white;&quot;&gt;#LI-Hybrid&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Datadog offers a competitive salary and equity package, and may include variable compensation. Actual compensation is based on factors such as the candidate&#39;s skills, qualifications, and experience. In addition, Datadog offers a wide range of best in class, comprehensive and inclusive employee benefits for this role including healthcare, dental, parental planning, and mental health benefits, a 401(k) plan and match, paid time off, fitness reimbursements, and a discounted employee stock purchase plan.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;The reasonably estimated yearly salary for this role at Datadog is:&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$187,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$240,000 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Datadog:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Datadog (NASDAQ: DDOG) is a global SaaS business, delivering a rare combination of growth and profitability. We are on a mission to break down silos and solve complexity in the cloud age by enabling digital transformation, cloud migration, and infrastructure monitoring of our customers’ entire technology stacks. Built by engineers, for engineers, Datadog is used by organizations of all sizes across a wide range of industries. Together, we champion professional development, diversity of thought, innovation, and work excellence to empower continuous growth. Join the pack and become part of a collaborative, pragmatic, and thoughtful people-first community where we solve tough problems, take smart risks, and celebrate one another. Learn more about #DatadogLife on &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.instagram.com/datadoghq/?hl=en&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Instagram&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.linkedin.com/company/datadog&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;LinkedIn,&lt;/a&gt; and &lt;a href=&quot;https://learn.datadoghq.com/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Datadog Learning Center. &lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;p data-renderer-start-pos=&quot;215&quot;&gt;&lt;strong data-renderer-mark=&quot;true&quot;&gt;Equal Opportunity at Datadog:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Datadog is proud to offer &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.eeoc.gov/sites/default/files/2023-06/22-088_EEOC_KnowYourRights6.12ScreenRdr.pdf&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;equal employment opportunity&lt;/a&gt; to everyone regardless of race, color, ancestry, religion, sex, national origin, sexual orientation, age, citizenship, marital status, disability, gender identity, veteran status, and other characteristics protected by law. We also consider qualified applicants regardless of criminal histories, consistent with legal requirements. Here are our &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.datadoghq.com/legal/candidate-legal-notices/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Candidate Legal Notices&lt;/a&gt; for your reference.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Datadog endeavors to make our Careers Page accessible to all users. If you would like to contact us regarding the accessibility of our website or need assistance completing the application process, please complete &lt;a href=&quot;https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSeoJeduEZ2NdZF_65uZmWUrCM-zee7yADXX1s6Xr9zAGq8iKA/viewform&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;this form&lt;/a&gt;. This form is for accommodation requests only and cannot be used to inquire about the status of applications.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-renderer-start-pos=&quot;662&quot;&gt;&lt;strong data-renderer-mark=&quot;true&quot;&gt;Privacy and AI Guidelines:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-renderer-start-pos=&quot;662&quot;&gt;Any information you submit to Datadog as part of your application will be processed in accordance with Datadog’s&amp;nbsp;&lt;a class=&quot;c-link&quot; href=&quot;https://www.datadoghq.com/legal/applicant-candidate-privacy/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; data-stringify-link=&quot;https://www.datadoghq.com/legal/applicant-candidate-privacy/&quot; data-sk=&quot;tooltip_parent&quot;&gt;Applicant and Candidate Privacy Notice&lt;/a&gt;. For information on our AI policy, please visit &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.datadoghq.com/legal/interviewing-at-datadog-ai-guidelines/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Interviewing at Datadog AI Guidelines&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Datadog is seeking a skilled and adaptable Contracts Manager to join its growing Legal team. In this role, you will be responsible for drafting, reviewing, and negotiating a diverse range of vendor contracts. This role operates within established playbooks, contract templates, and/or risk frameworks across Datadog’s vendor ecosystem, with non-standard or higher-risk issues escalated to senior legal team members. You will also contribute to process improvements that support efficient and consistent contracting practices.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;At Datadog, we place value in our office culture - the relationships and collaboration it builds and the creativity it brings to the table. We operate as a hybrid workplace to ensure our Datadogs can create a work-life harmony that best fits them.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You’ll Do:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work closely with the Legal team and serve as a key point of contact for Procurement and internal stakeholders, supporting supplier and service provider engagements under established legal guidance. Responsibilities cover the full contract lifecycle from intake and negotiation through execution, amendment, and end-of-life.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Review, draft, and negotiate a range of standard buy-side commercial agreements, with an emphasis on SaaS and technology-related vendor transactions. Typical intake may include agreements covering software, cloud services, privacy, professional services and consulting, marketing and advertising, equipment agreements (purchase, rental, and maintenance), office operations, facilities, and benefits.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner cross-functionally with business stakeholders and subject-matter experts, including Product, Privacy, Security, and Procurement, to identify gaps between proposed contract terms and business, technical, and compliance requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support vendor dispute resolution efforts by gathering information and coordinating with legal and business stakeholders.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support and advise on contract renewals and amendments, and provide practical guidance to internal teams regarding rights, obligations, and risk exposure under existing agreements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to the development, enhancement, and ongoing maintenance of contract templates, negotiation playbooks, and scalable self-service resources.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with the Legal Operations team to support and optimize the Legal Department’s use of technology, including contract lifecycle management (CLM) systems and AI-assisted contract review tools.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participate in cross-functional projects and continuous improvement initiatives to advance the Legal Department and company-wide objectives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;Who You Are:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A contracts professional with at least 5 years of experience reviewing, redlining, negotiating, and advising on a broad range of commercial agreements, with a working knowledge of data privacy and security issues related to technology, benefits, marketing and other vendor agreements. Experience with real estate contracting and vendor dispute resolution is a plus, but not required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Able to manage standard contract work with limited guidance, exercising sound judgment in day-to-day decision making, and appropriately escalating non-standard or higher-risk issues when legal, commercial, or other considerations warrant broader review.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to identify legal, operational, and business risk in proposed contract terms, clearly explain those risks to internal stakeholders, and propose alternative language consistent with established guidance, escalating as needed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A problem solver who can identify efficiency and scalability opportunities and collaborate with senior team members on the implementation of process improvements.&amp;nbsp; This may include supporting the development of self-service resources, training materials, playbooks, and related workflow improvements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Organized, process-driven, and resourceful, with strong attention to detail and the ability to manage multiple matters simultaneously.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Curious and adaptable, with a desire to learn and an aptitude for technology and legal operations tools.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A strong written and verbal communicator with excellent interpersonal skills and a demonstrated ability to collaborate across functions and remain effective in fast-paced or high-pressure situations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Flexible and eager to operate in a dynamic, deadline-driven environment, with a mindset that no task is too big or too small.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Datadog values people from all walks of life. We understand not everyone will meet all the above qualifications on day one. That&#39;s okay. If you’re passionate about technology and want to grow your skills, we encourage you to apply.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
