&lt;p&gt;Datadog is the leading AI-powered observability and security platform for cloud applications. We serve a vibrant community of developers and engineers and we pride ourselves on communicating with them in clear and authentic ways.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are seeking a dynamic, strategic, and hands-on Communications Manager to support Datadog’s corporate communication efforts in the US and support global product communications and social media efforts as needed.&lt;br&gt;We are looking for a proven corporate communications professional who has experience in supporting fast-growing companies &lt;em&gt;and&lt;/em&gt; fast-growing global communications teams.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The ideal candidate thrives in building not only communications strategies – but also operations and ways of working that support a growing global communications team. This means you understand how to quickly identify process gaps, enjoy developing scalable solutions and are nimble when working with a global team.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This person is happy to roll up their sleeves to not only develop impactful US communications strategies, but also to help drive execution on global efforts as needed. Reporting directly to the Head of Global of Corporate Communications, this person will help drive key aspects of Datadog’s US corporate communications strategy and work closely with key stakeholders across the company.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;At Datadog, we place value in our office culture - the relationships and collaboration it builds, and the creativity it brings to the table. We operate as a hybrid workplace to ensure our Datadogs can create a work-life harmony that best fits them.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You Will Do:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and execute communication strategies to enhance brand visibility and reputation in the US.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead complex communication projects and campaigns, ensuring alignment with business objectives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build mechanisms and processes to help support a growing global communications function.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage day-to-day operations and be a go-to contact for our external US PR agency.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with cross-functional teams—including Investor Relations, Legal, Event Marketing, Partner Marketing, Customer Marketing, Community and Advocacy—to drive and amplify news.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track and report on relevant company news coverage in the US.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Draft, edit and approve media comments, briefing materials, op-eds and press releases.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Draft, edit and publish posts on Datadog&#39;s corporate social media channels across LinkedIn, X, Facebook and Instagram, as needed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Position Datadog executives and subject matter experts as thought leaders in the industry through bylined articles, speaking engagements and media interviews.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor industry trends, media coverage, and competitive landscape to inform PR strategies and proactively shape narratives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who You Are:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree with 4-6 years of related communications experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven success building and executing corporate communication strategies for fast-growing technology companies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong experience working with global PR agencies.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep understanding of traditional and social media trends.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience developing and driving communications campaigns for B2B companies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional project management, written, verbal, and presentation skills; meticulous attention to detail.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable working in a fast-paced, high-growth environment with shifting priorities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;p1&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;Datadog values people from all walks of life. We understand not everyone will meet all the above qualifications on day one. That&#39;s okay. If you’re passionate about technology and want to grow your skills, we encourage you to apply.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
