&lt;p&gt;As a Product Manager II on the Code Security team, you will lead the charge in defining and executing Datadog’s roadmap for securing the software supply chain in the era of AI-assisted and agentic coding. This is a strategic and technical role focused on identifying emerging risks in modern development workflows and translating those insights into high-impact product capabilities. You’ll work cross-functionally with engineering, security research, design, and go-to-market teams to launch innovative solutions that help customers stay ahead of evolving threats. This role offers a unique opportunity to grow your expertise in both application security and AI, while shaping one of Datadog’s fastest-growing product areas.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;At Datadog, we place value in our office culture - the relationships that it builds, the creativity it brings to the table, and the collaboration of being together. We operate as a hybrid workplace to ensure our employees can create a work-life harmony that best fits them.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You’ll Do:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the product roadmap for AI native software supply chain security, defining how Datadog supports customers as AI coding tools reshape the SDLC&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conduct deep customer discovery with security and engineering teams to uncover critical gaps in vulnerability management, supply chain protection, and AI-assisted coding workflows&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate cross-functionally with engineering, design, security research, and go-to-market teams to drive alignment and execute on roadmap priorities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Launch new capabilities from 0 to 1, helping to establish and grow the Code Security portfolio’s presence in the market&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate complex technical challenges into clear product strategies that address customer needs and market opportunities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who You Are:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have 3+ years of experience as a Product Manager owning the roadmap and execution for technical products, ideally in developer tools, security, or infrastructure&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You enjoy engaging directly with customers, leading discovery calls, participating in sales conversations, and building relationships to understand user needs&lt;br&gt;You have a solid technical understanding of the software development lifecycle (SDLC), including how security integrates into modern developer workflows&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are familiar with AI coding tools or agentic development workflows and are comfortable working at the intersection of AI and security&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You thrive in cross-functional environments and enjoy turning ambiguous problems into tangible product outcomes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have experience taking new features or products from 0 to 1, making thoughtful tradeoffs about what to build (and what not to build) in fast paced environments&lt;/li&gt;
