&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Datadog:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re on a mission to build the best platform in the world for engineers, operations, and security teams to understand, secure, and scale their systems, applications, and teams. We operate at high scale—trillions of data points per day, allowing for seamless collaboration and problem-solving among DevOps and Security teams globally for tens of thousands of companies. Our engineering culture values pragmatism, honesty, and simplicity to solve hard problems the right way.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Team:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Logs are one of the richest sources of operational, security, and business data: powering use cases such as troubleshooting, threat detection, high volume log optimization, business transaction monitoring, and compliance. We&#39;re looking for a Product Manager II to help build the next generation of AI-powered log management capabilities. Our vision is to make it radically faster and easier for engineers, operators, and security teams to ingest, explore, and extract actionable insights from petabytes of log data using AI-first experiences.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll work across the log lifecycle, from ingestion and processing pipelines to exploration and analytics, partnering with engineering, design, and data science to ship features that leverage agentic AI, natural language querying, and intelligent automation to transform how customers interact with their logs.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;At Datadog, we place value in our office culture - the relationships and collaboration it builds and the creativity it brings to the table. We operate as a hybrid workplace to ensure our Datadogs can create a work-life harmony that best fits them.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Do:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop a deep understanding of the day-to-day life of infrastructure, operations, and security teams that rely on logs to measure the health, performance, and security posture of their systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify and prioritize high-impact use cases where AI-driven log analytics can deliver outsized customer value,&amp;nbsp; such as intelligent log pattern detection, anomaly identification, AI-assisted root cause analysis, and natural language querying.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define and build experiences that combine Agentic AI, Workflows, and Analytics to create next-generation investigation and remediation runbooks for operations and security teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with engineering, design, and data science teams to build and iterate on AI-driven insights, automation, and workflow applications on top of log data.&lt;/li&gt;
