&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for a strategic and collaborative Senior Group Manager to lead a lean, high-impact Customer Marketing team at Datadog. In this role, you’ll mentor and manage a group of marketers while also driving programs that highlight customer success, elevate market reputation, and enable go-to-market teams with compelling customer stories. You’ll balance team leadership with program ownership and cross-functional execution, helping bring the voice of the customer to the center of our brand strategy.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Datadog, we place value in our office culture - the relationships and collaboration it builds and the creativity it brings to the table. We operate as a hybrid workplace to ensure our Datadogs can create a work-life harmony that best fits them. This role is based in New York or San Francisco.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You’ll Do:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage and mentor a lean, high-performing Customer Marketing team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with Product Marketing, Sales, and Customer Success to identify reference opportunities and create customer-ready assets&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Orchestrate end-to-end production of customer case studies, videos, and quotes—including budgeting, team resourcing, and coordination with partners such as Events Marketing, Corporate Communications, and Analyst Relations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Execute and report on always-on market reputation and peer review campaigns for platforms like Gartner Peer Insights and G2&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with geographic and market segment leaders to align budget and team resources with business objectives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stand up and amplify internal communication channels and content promotion to increase use of assets and drive pipeline&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who You Are:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years of experience in customer marketing roles, with a proven track record of team management in high-growth technology environments; B2B software experience is a plus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree or equivalent experience required; MBA is a plus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated success working cross-functionally to source, develop, and amplify customer stories across internal and external channels&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Skilled at leading customer-facing conversations and navigating legal, operational, and production processes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong operational acumen with the ability to accelerate content creation, improve efficiency, and report on ROI&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experienced in managing and growing small teams with broad scope and impact&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep understanding of customer marketing trends, best practices, and tools&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Datadog values people from all walks of life. We understand not everyone will meet all the above qualifications on day one. That&#39;s okay. If you’re passionate about technology and want to grow your skills, we encourage you to apply.&lt;/p&gt;
