&lt;p&gt;Datadog is seeking a Staff Product Manager to help lead and scale our OpenTelemetry efforts across Datadog products.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;OpenTelemetry is foundational to modern observability and Datadog already provides a strong set of OpenTelemetry capabilities to power standards-based observability experiences for customers. In this highly visible role, you will evolve OpenTelemetry at Datadog, strengthening consistency, deepening integration, and delivering best-in-class experiences for customers who rely on open standards.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will partner closely with cross-functional teams to ensure OpenTelemetry is a seamless and powerful path for sending, managing, and analyzing telemetry in Datadog. This role requires both strategic thinking and hands-on execution, operating at the intersection of open source technology and business.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;At Datadog, we place value in our office culture - the relationships and collaboration it builds and the creativity it brings to the table. We operate as a hybrid workplace to ensure our Datadogs can create a work-life harmony that best fits them.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You’ll Do:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define and drive Datadog’s company-wide OpenTelemetry vision and roadmap, ensuring consistent and high-quality OpenTelemetry support across products.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive customer discovery across multiple products and initiatives, synthesizing insights from customer conversations, supporting data, and the OpenTelemetry community.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with product and engineering leaders across product portfolio to strengthen native OpenTelemetry support across all signals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Influence OpenTelemetry investment direction and product priorities by connecting customer needs and observability trends with business opportunities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define and track internal and external OpenTelemetry adoption metrics, communicating progress and impact to leadership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Represent Datadog externally with customers and in industry forums, contributing to thought leadership around observability standards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who You Are:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8+ years of Product Management experience, with significant ownership in infrastructure, observability, telemetry systems, or developer platforms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong technical understanding of distributed systems, agents/collectors, libraries, telemetry pipelines, and the OpenTelemetry ecosystem.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A systems thinker who can connect ingestion architecture, platform capabilities, and end-user experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading large, cross-functional initiatives across multiple product areas.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communicator with the ability to influence senior engineering, design, and go-to-market stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Customer-focused and data-driven in your decision-making.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
