&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;End to end ownership and accountability for new business strategy across Figma Weave&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Attract, hire and retain the best commercial talent to scale the Figma Weave Sales Team. Build a team with varied strengths, create and cultivate an environment of belonging&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participate in customer and prospect meetings; you’re someone who loves getting in front of customers and coaching your team&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be passionate about career development and coaching&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bring strong sales excellence, process and methodology as we expand and scale the business.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead weekly forecast meetings and mentor the Sales team on strategies to help exceed their goals&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with and provide insight to the Executive team on the needs of the team and the market&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate closely with the marketing and product teams to ensure they understand and can service the needs of the market and members in the region&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We&#39;d love to hear from you if you have:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years of sales experience (preferably within SaaS) with 3+ years of management experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience selling with an Enterprise book of customers (5000+ FTEs) and selling to executives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven track record of leading successful and consistent sales team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understanding of our technical and competitive landscape&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to thrive in a constantly changing and evolving environment&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excitement for increasing customer happiness and developing lasting customer relationships&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
