&lt;p&gt;This is a full time role that can be held from one of our US hubs or remotely in the United States.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;What you’ll do at Figma:&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead U.S. international tax planning and structuring initiatives, including M&amp;amp;A transactions, cross-border investments, expansion into new jurisdictions, and OECD Pillar Two readiness&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own U.S. international tax provision calculations under ASC 740, including GILTI, Subpart F, foreign tax credits, and related international components of quarterly and annual reporting&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead U.S. international tax compliance and information reporting (e.g., Forms 5471, 8858, 8991–8993, 1118), partnering with external advisors to ensure accurate and timely filings&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be responsible for intercompany transactions and global transfer pricing policies to support compliance and operational efficiency&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor global tax legislative developments, model potential impacts, and communicate recommendations to finance leadership and cross-functional partners&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support tax-efficient repatriation strategies and other international tax planning initiatives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as a technical resource for audits, special projects, and cross-functional tax matter&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;section page-centered&quot;&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;We&#39;d love to hear from you if you have:&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;6+ years of U.S. international tax experience, including Big 4 and/or in-house experience at a multinational company&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated experience applying ASC 740 and U.S. international tax rules (e.g., GILTI, Subpart F, foreign tax credits, transfer pricing) in a multinational environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience preparing or reviewing U.S. international information returns, including Forms 5471 and 8858&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience preparing or reviewing international components of quarterly and annual tax provisions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;While not required, it’s an added plus if you also have:&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with OECD Pillar Two modeling, readiness, or implementation&lt;/li&gt;
