&lt;p&gt;This is a full time role that can be held from one of our US hubs or remotely in the United States.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you&#39;ll do at Figma:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage and support a team of experienced engineers to drive design systems usage across Figma’s product suite, with a goal of growing the team in 2026&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with product and design leadership to set the strategy, priorities, and mission for the team and roadmap&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Roll up your sleeves to provide technical leadership of the team, including supporting their technical decisions and growth of team members&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build a collaborative culture of doing great work together, by investing in direct mentorship, shaping team practices, and helping guide the team towards meaningful work&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Grow your career in a collaborative and creative engineering community&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We’d love to hear from you if you have:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;4+ years of engineering management experience, including 2+ years of manager of manager experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8+ years of product engineering experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Built high-performing and highly engaged engineering teams through hiring and growing people&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven track record of building and shipping beloved and high-quality products&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A deep passion for design craft and usability&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;While it’s not required, it’s an added plus if you also have:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building in especially complex product spaces, with goals of making the product as simple and usable as possible&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
