&lt;p&gt;GitLab is proud to be an equal opportunity workplace and is an affirmative action employer. GitLab’s policies and practices relating to recruitment, employment, career development and advancement, promotion, and retirement are based solely on merit, regardless of race, color, religion, ancestry, sex (including pregnancy, lactation, sexual orientation, gender identity, or gender expression), national origin, age, citizenship, marital status, mental or physical disability, genetic information (including family medical history), discharge status from the military, protected veteran status (which includes disabled veterans, recently separated veterans, active duty wartime or campaign badge veterans, and Armed Forces service medal veterans), or any other basis protected by law. GitLab will not tolerate discrimination or harassment based on any of these characteristics. See also&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://about.gitlab.com/handbook/people-policies/inc-usa/#equal-employment-opportunity-policy&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;GitLab’s EEO Policy&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;and&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://about.gitlab.com/handbook/labor-and-employment-notices/#eeoc-us-equal-employment-opportunity-commission-notices&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;EEO is the Law&lt;/a&gt;. If you have a disability or special need that requires&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://about.gitlab.com/handbook/people-policies/inc-usa/#reasonable-accommodation&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;accommodation&lt;/a&gt;, please let us know during the&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://about.gitlab.com/handbook/hiring/interviewing/#adjustments-to-our-interview-process&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;recruiting process&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;GitLab is the intelligent orchestration platform for DevSecOps. GitLab enables organizations to increase developer productivity, improve operational efficiency, reduce security and compliance risk, and accelerate digital transformation. More than 50 million registered users and more than 50% of the Fortune 100* trust GitLab to ship better, more secure software faster.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The same principles built into our products are reflected in how our team works: we embrace AI as a core productivity multiplier, with all team members expected to incorporate AI into their daily workflows to drive efficiency, innovation, and impact. GitLab is where careers accelerate, innovation flourishes, and every voice is valued. Our high-performance culture is driven by our &lt;a href=&quot;https://handbook.gitlab.com/handbook/values/&quot;&gt;values&lt;/a&gt; and continuous knowledge exchange, enabling our team members to reach their full potential while collaborating with industry leaders to solve complex problems. &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=OuZIb5zszQI&quot;&gt;Co-create the future with us&lt;/a&gt; as we build technology that transforms how the world develops software.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;*&lt;em&gt;Fortune 500® is a registered trademark of Fortune Media IP Limited, used under license. Claim based on GitLab data. Fortune 100 refers to the top 20% ranked companies in the 2025 Fortune 500 list, published in June 2025. Fortune and Fortune Media IP Limited are not affiliated with, and do not endorse products or services of GitLab.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;An overview of this role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As an Executive Business Administrator, you&#39;ll provide strategic, high-impact support to four senior leaders in GitLab&#39;s People Group: the VP of Total Rewards, VP of Talent Acquisition, VP of People Strategy and Engagement, and VP of Diversity, Inclusion, and Belonging. You&#39;ll create leverage for these executives by managing complex calendars and travel across time zones, planning key team events, supporting recruiting and onboarding activities, and staying ahead of what&#39;s needed so they can focus on leading and scaling our GitLab team. You&#39;ll work primarily across Google Workspace, Slack, Zoom, Navan, and GitLab, toggling between them with ease while identifying priorities, resolving conflicts, and escalating urgent issues when needed. In your first year, you&#39;ll establish trusted partnerships with each VP, bring consistency and reliability to their operations, and contribute to the broader EBA community by sharing best practices and stepping in to support other executives when required.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You’ll Do&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support and partner closely with four People Group executives (Total Rewards, Talent Acquisition, People Strategy and Engagement, and Diversity, Inclusion and Belonging) while flexing to shifting priorities across their teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own and proactively manage complex, high-volume calendars across multiple time zones, ensuring time is aligned to strategic priorities and key deliverables.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate extensive domestic and non-US travel end to end, including transportation, lodging, visas, and documentation, and accompany executives when needed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Plan and execute events such as team off-sites, large meetings, team building activities, and company kick-offs in partnership with cross-functional stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support the full recruiting lifecycle for the People Group by scheduling interviews, coordinating with candidates and hiring teams, and helping organize onboarding activities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Compile and submit timely, accurate expense reports and support related processes such as purchase orders using tools like Google Workspace, Navan, Zoom, and Slack.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide coverage and backup for other Executive Business Administrators, sharing best practices and helping drive consistency across the EBA community.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Run and lead special projects and ad hoc initiatives for People Group executives, taking ownership from scoping through follow-up while communicating clearly with partners.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You’ll Bring&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience providing executive-level administrative support in a dynamic, fast-paced environment, ideally partnering with People, Product, or Engineering leaders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency with Google Workspace, Zoom, Slack, Navan, and related tools and processes such as purchase orders, with the ability to quickly learn new technical tools.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to manage complex, frequently changing calendars and travel across multiple time zones, and to plan and coordinate events such as off-sites and large meetings.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated experience working independently, moving quickly between tasks, and using sound judgment to prioritize, solve problems, and anticipate executive needs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;History of building strong, collaborative relationships across teams, including partnering effectively with other Executive Business Administrators and stakeholders at all levels.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supporting recruiting activities, including coordinating interviews, liaising between candidates and hiring teams, and assisting with onboarding logistics.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong organizational and communication skills with attention to detail, including preparing accurate expense reports and handling sensitive information with discretion.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Openness to working in an all-remote, distributed environment, with a sincere willingness to help others and contribute to a positive, &quot;one team&quot; culture; diverse and transferable experience is valued.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Executive Business Administrator will join GitLab&#39;s People Group and includes Total Rewards, Talent Acquisition, People Strategy and Engagement, and Diversity, Inclusion, and Belonging. This distributed group partners across GitLab to attract, support, and retain team members while building an inclusive, values-aligned culture. You&#39;ll be part of a broader community of EBAs who collaborate asynchronously across time zones using GitLab, Google Workspace, Slack, and Zoom to stay aligned, share knowledge, and provide continuous coverage. The team is focused on scaling people programs, improving processes, and enabling senior People leaders to spend more time on strategic work that supports GitLab&#39;s mission and growth.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;How GitLab will support you&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://about.gitlab.com/handbook/total-rewards/benefits/general-and-entity-benefits/&quot;&gt;Benefits to support your health, finances, and well-being&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://handbook.gitlab.com/handbook/people-group/paid-time-off/&quot;&gt;Flexible Paid Time Off&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://about.gitlab.com/company/culture/inclusion/erg-guide/#:~:text=Definition%20of%20the%20TMRG%20%2D%20Team%20Member%20Resource%20Groups,-TMRGs%20are%20voluntary&amp;amp;text=The%20purpose%20for%20this%20type,developing%20the%20sense%20of%20belonging.&quot;&gt;Team Member Resource Groups&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://handbook.gitlab.com/handbook/total-rewards/stock-options/&quot;&gt;Equity Compensation &amp;amp; Employee Stock Purchase Plan&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://handbook.gitlab.com/handbook/people-group/learning-and-development/growth-and-development/&quot;&gt;Growth and Development Fund&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://about.gitlab.com/handbook/total-rewards/benefits/general-and-entity-benefits/#parental-leave&quot;&gt;Parental leave&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://handbook.gitlab.com/handbook/finance/expenses/#equipment&quot;&gt;Home office&lt;/a&gt; support&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Please note that we welcome interest from candidates with varying levels of experience; many successful candidates do not meet every single requirement. Additionally, studies have shown that people from &lt;a href=&quot;https://about.gitlab.com/company/culture/inclusion/#examples-of-select-underrepresented-groups&quot;&gt;underrepresented groups&lt;/a&gt; are less likely to apply to a job unless they meet every single qualification. If you&#39;re excited about this role, please apply and allow our recruiters to assess your application.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
