&lt;p&gt;GitLab is proud to be an equal opportunity workplace and is an affirmative action employer. GitLab’s policies and practices relating to recruitment, employment, career development and advancement, promotion, and retirement are based solely on merit, regardless of race, color, religion, ancestry, sex (including pregnancy, lactation, sexual orientation, gender identity, or gender expression), national origin, age, citizenship, marital status, mental or physical disability, genetic information (including family medical history), discharge status from the military, protected veteran status (which includes disabled veterans, recently separated veterans, active duty wartime or campaign badge veterans, and Armed Forces service medal veterans), or any other basis protected by law. GitLab will not tolerate discrimination or harassment based on any of these characteristics. See also&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://about.gitlab.com/handbook/people-policies/inc-usa/#equal-employment-opportunity-policy&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;GitLab’s EEO Policy&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;and&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://about.gitlab.com/handbook/labor-and-employment-notices/#eeoc-us-equal-employment-opportunity-commission-notices&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;EEO is the Law&lt;/a&gt;. If you have a disability or special need that requires&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://about.gitlab.com/handbook/people-policies/inc-usa/#reasonable-accommodation&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;accommodation&lt;/a&gt;, please let us know during the&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://about.gitlab.com/handbook/hiring/interviewing/#adjustments-to-our-interview-process&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;recruiting process&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;GitLab is the intelligent orchestration platform for DevSecOps. GitLab enables organizations to increase developer productivity, improve operational efficiency, reduce security and compliance risk, and accelerate digital transformation. More than 50 million registered users and more than 50% of the Fortune 100* trust GitLab to ship better, more secure software faster.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The same principles built into our products are reflected in how our team works: we embrace AI as a core productivity multiplier, with all team members expected to incorporate AI into their daily workflows to drive efficiency, innovation, and impact. GitLab is where careers accelerate, innovation flourishes, and every voice is valued. Our high-performance culture is driven by our &lt;a href=&quot;https://handbook.gitlab.com/handbook/values/&quot;&gt;values&lt;/a&gt; and continuous knowledge exchange, enabling our team members to reach their full potential while collaborating with industry leaders to solve complex problems. &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=OuZIb5zszQI&quot;&gt;Co-create the future with us&lt;/a&gt; as we build technology that transforms how the world develops software.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;*&lt;em&gt;Fortune 500® is a registered trademark of Fortune Media IP Limited, used under license. Claim based on GitLab data. Fortune 100 refers to the top 20% ranked companies in the 2025 Fortune 500 list, published in June 2025. Fortune and Fortune Media IP Limited are not affiliated with, and do not endorse products or services of GitLab.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;An overview of this role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Sales Commission Analyst, you&#39;ll help ensure that GitLab&#39;s sales incentives are accurate, transparent, and aligned with how we support customers. You&#39;ll own day-to-day commission calculations, reporting, and first-tier end user support so sales team members are paid correctly and can trust the data that guides their performance. You&#39;ll work closely with Sales and Sales Operations, use incentive compensation tools and SFDC to research and resolve compensation questions, and continuously improve processes to make our commission operations more efficient and compliant, including supporting SOX-related documentation and reporting.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You’ll Do&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li value=&quot;1&quot;&gt;Execute accurate worldwide sales commission calculations, reporting, and first-tier end user support using compensation analytics tools.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li value=&quot;2&quot;&gt;Investigate and resolve compensation issues by tracking, researching, and providing clear analysis to stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li value=&quot;3&quot;&gt;Interpret and apply all sales compensation plans, ensuring calculations are correct and plan participants are accurately credited for their transactions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li value=&quot;4&quot;&gt;Track and report on commission plan acceptance and related documentation to support compliance and timeliness.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li value=&quot;5&quot;&gt;Partner with Sales, Sales Operations, and Finance to validate data, clarify policies, and align on compensation decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li value=&quot;6&quot;&gt;Identify, recommend, and implement process improvements that increase efficiency and reduce manual work in commission operations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li value=&quot;7&quot;&gt;Support SOX compliance through thorough documentation, controls testing support, and audit-ready reporting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li value=&quot;8&quot;&gt;Prepare ad hoc analyses and contribute to projects that enhance the effectiveness and scalability of GitLab&#39;s sales incentive programs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You’ll Bring&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li value=&quot;1&quot;&gt;Background in accounting, finance, economics, or another quantitative field, or equivalent practical experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li value=&quot;2&quot;&gt;Experience working with sales incentive programs, including understanding of compensation plans, processes, and procedures&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li value=&quot;2&quot;&gt;Experience as an Xactly Incent administrator or power user, with the ability to configure plans, validate commissions, and optimize system performance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li value=&quot;3&quot;&gt;Proficiency interpreting, analyzing, and validating data to support accurate commission calculations and reporting&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li value=&quot;4&quot;&gt;Strong attention to detail, with a structured, self-directed approach to problem solving and organization&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li value=&quot;5&quot;&gt;Clear written and verbal communication skills, with the ability to explain findings and resolve issues with cross-functional partners&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li value=&quot;6&quot;&gt;Hands-on experience with Salesforce (SFDC), Google Workspace, and an incentive compensation management tool&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li value=&quot;7&quot;&gt;Familiarity with SaaS and B2B sales environments and related sales operations practices&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li value=&quot;8&quot;&gt;Interest in GitLab and open source software, alignment with GitLab&#39;s values, and willingness to learn and use GitLab in day-to-day work&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll join a small, specialized team that supports Sales and Sales Operations by managing the end-to-end sales commission process, from plan execution through analytics and compliance. The team works across functions such as Finance, Revenue Operations, and Sales leadership to ensure commission plans are understood, implemented accurately, and reflected correctly in downstream systems. As part of GitLab&#39;s all-remote, globally distributed team, you&#39;ll collaborate asynchronously with colleagues in multiple regions using GitLab and Google Workspace to document processes, share analysis, and drive continuous improvements to how we calculate, report, and govern sales incentives.&lt;/p&gt;
