&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Guidepoint’s Human Resources team thrives on problem solving and creating happier employees. As Guidepoint works to achieve its mission of making individuals, businesses, and the world smarter through personalized knowledge-sharing solutions, the NYC office is looking for a Talent Development Manager to champion the company’s efforts to attract, develop and retain talent globally. This position requires a minimum of two days in office attendance with flexibility to work on site additional days when needed.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;After a few months on the job: As Guidepoint’s Talent Development Manager, you will embrace the opportunity to shape a high-performing organization, using your sound ideas and management skills to create and implement learning programs that help employees contribute at their full potential.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
