&lt;p&gt;Join the team as Twilio’s next Enterprise Architect.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the job&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This position is needed to transform our data ecosystem by designing and implementing a unified, governed data architecture across the company. This role is accountable for the technical rationalization of disparate data lakes, ensuring rigorous governance, and compelling cross-functional teams to adopt standardized, centralized data tooling.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Enterprise Architect responsible for the Enterprise Data Domain defines and executes the data strategy, determining the future state of our data ecosystem and bears accountability for its long-term viability.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In this role, you’ll:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Formulate the enterprise-wide data strategy to align with long-term business objectives and forecast future technological requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design scalable data architectures that integrate heterogeneous data sources. Ensure all designs adhere strictly to enterprise security and compliance standards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Author the policies that govern data access, retention, and sovereignty globally. Establish the enforcement mechanisms&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Implement rigorous data governance frameworks. Define ownership, stewardship, and quality metrics for data residing in disparate lakes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Audit the current portfolio of data tools. Identify redundancies and execute plans to decommission inferior software, thereby reducing technical debt.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analyze existing data silos. Engineer integration patterns that expose trapped data to the broader enterprise without compromising integrity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Confront business leaders with technical realities. Articulate the cost of sprawl and the value of a unified data model.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Twilio values diverse experiences from all kinds of industries, and we encourage everyone who meets the required qualifications to apply. If your career is just starting or hasn&#39;t followed a traditional path, don&#39;t let that stop you from considering Twilio. We are always looking for people who will bring something new to the table!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;*Required:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Minimum 12 years in enterprise technology or data, with at least 5 years dedicated to data architecture.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Data Warehousing Methodologies: &lt;/strong&gt;Both TOGAF certification and demonstrated thought leadership in convincing executives to invest in the formalism of full data lifecycle specific to Data Warehousing engineering and governance.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Technical Leadership:&lt;/strong&gt; Deep, hands-on expertise in building architecture and engineering practices around any leading Data Warehouse&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Database Strategy:&lt;/strong&gt; Proven mastery in rationalizing complex estates containing disparate relational and non-relational database system including proven track record of operationalizing data governance in complex environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Leadership:&lt;/strong&gt; Demonstrated ability to influence C-level executives and steer large organizations without direct HR authority.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Complex Rationalization:&lt;/strong&gt; History of successfully merging multi-national or mulit-line-of-business data estates during M&amp;amp;A activities or massive re-organizations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Desired:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Recent, hands on technical experience with any of the following: Snowflake, AWS, Informatica, dbt, Datahub, and Presto, Datahub/Acryl&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Master’s degree in a quantitative field strongly preferred&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
