&lt;p&gt;Join the team as our Marketing Campaigns Intern on Twilio’s EMEA Marketing team for a duration of 12 weeks, starting on 8th June.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the internship&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Twilio is seeking a Marketing Campaigns Intern to join our EMEA Marketing team and support the delivery of integrated campaigns focused on customer acquisition. This is a fantastic opportunity for a collaborative individual to gain hands-on experience in a fast-paced environment, assisting with the execution and optimisation of global campaigns as well as regional programs that deliver real business impact.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The ideal candidate possesses a &quot;start-up&quot; mentality and a passion for learning how to convert prospects into qualified leads through multi-channel campaigns tactics. Working alongside the regional campaigns team, you will help adapt global strategies for regional needs while developing the fundamental skills required for a successful career in marketing.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In this role, you will:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support Campaign Execution: Assist in the development and rollout of integrated marketing campaigns, helping to localise content and track deliverables against regional timelines.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stakeholder Coordination: Provide support to key partners in Demand Generation and Field Marketing teams to ensure campaign messaging and assets are delivered and performing effectively.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Reporting &amp;amp; Performance Support: Assist in collecting data to track individual initiative milestones and help prepare campaign updates for stakeholders, contributing to the development of &quot;test &amp;amp; learn&quot; strategies to ensure regional ROI metrics are met.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Content &amp;amp; Creative Support: Coordinate with internal teams and agencies to track the production of campaign assets, ensuring all deadlines are met.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Twilio values diverse experiences, and we encourage students from various backgrounds to apply. We are looking for individuals who bring a fresh perspective and a hunger to learn.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Currently enrolled in a Bachelors or Masters degree in Marketing, Business or Communications (or equivalent experience).&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Foundational Marketing Knowledge: Requires an understanding of core campaign components, including the integration of adjacent marketing functions and tactics.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong Organisational Skills: Ability to manage multiple small tasks or projects simultaneously with high attention to detail.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborative Spirit: A team-player mentality with the ability to build effective working relationships in a remote environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Communication Skills: Excellent verbal and written communication skills in English.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Desired:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Tech Savvy: Familiarity with or a strong desire to master industry-standard tools (e.g., Salesforce, Adobe Experience Manager, and Canva), combined with a proactive curiosity for emerging AI technologies to streamline content creation, automate task management, and drive campaign optimisation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Growth Mindset: A &quot;test and learn&quot; attitude with a natural curiosity for analysing data and business performance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Agility: An energetic, self-motivated individual who thrives in a fast-paced &quot;start-up&quot; environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Multilingual: Proficiency in an additional European language applicable to the EMEA region&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role will be remote and based in the United Kingdom.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
