&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Schedule and perform regular H&amp;amp;S audits at each location.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure H&amp;amp;S compliance across all EMEA locations.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track corrective actions and ensure timely resolution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Emergency Preparedness &amp;amp; Response&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and test regional emergency response plans.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate drills and ensure all sites are prepared for emergencies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Data Collection &amp;amp; Reporting&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collect, analyze, and report on H&amp;amp;S metrics from all sites.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Present EMEA regional H&amp;amp;S performance to the GHS Manager&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Continuous Improvement&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify opportunities for process improvements and best practice sharing across sites.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead EMEA regional H&amp;amp;S initiatives and projects.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
