&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(255, 255, 255);&quot;&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;See yourself at Twilio&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Join the team as Twilio’s next &amp;nbsp;Solution Architect.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the job&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role will join Twilio’s Enterprise Applications Development &amp;amp; Operations organization as an Architect responsible for end-to-end architecture, delivery, and people leadership across Billing, AR, Collections, Cash Application, and Revenue Recognition platforms .&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The role operates at the intersection of technology, finance, and leadership. You will act as a hands-on architect and strategic owner for Twilio’s Q2C ecosystem, with deep expertise in Zuora Billing, Zuora Revenue (ASC 606) and ERP accounting flows.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will lead a team of engineers and functional specialists, partner closely with Finance, Accounting, Product, and Business Systems leaders, and ensure Twilio’s monetization platforms remain scalable, compliant, and resilient as the business grows through acquisitions, new pricing models, and global expansion.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;In this role, you’ll:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Architecture &amp;amp; Platform Ownership:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the end-to-end architecture for Billings-to-Cash, and Revenue platforms, including Zuora Billing, Zuora Revenue, ERP AR, payment gateways, tax engines, and downstream reporting systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design scalable, compliant solutions supporting subscriptions, usage-based billing, complex pricing, amendments, minimum commitments, and bundled offerings&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as the architecture authority for Q2C changes, ensuring alignment with ASC 606, SOX, audit, and internal control requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Delivery &amp;amp; Execution:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead design workshops, solution walkthroughs, and architecture reviews with business and finance stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate complex business requirements into robust functional and technical designs, End to end scenarios, Lucid flowcharts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversee delivery of enhancements, transformations, and compliance initiatives across Billing, AR, Revenue, and Cash processes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to influence executive-level decision-making through real-time technical analysis and spontaneous problem-solving, navigating through ambiguity&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive system conversions, migrations, and acquisitions onboarding into the Q2C landscape&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure high availability and operational excellence across production systems, including proactive monitoring and issue resolution&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Integration &amp;amp; Automation:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Govern integrations between Zuora, Salesforce CPQ/CRM, ERP (Oracle), tax engines, banks, payment gateways, usage mediation platforms, and reporting tools&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Champion automation and straight-through processing across billing, invoicing, revenue recognition, and close processes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure integrations follow enterprise integration standards, security controls, and performance benchmarks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Financial Close, Compliance &amp;amp; Reporting:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Accounting and Finance to support month-end close, reconciliations, audits, and regulatory reporting&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own system readiness for ASC 606 revenue accounting, deferred revenue, allocations, and satisfaction events&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Enable scalable reporting and analytics for Q2C KPIs, aging, revenue, and operational health&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Leadership &amp;amp; Talent Development:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead, and mentor a high-performing team of application engineers and functional SMEs , influence without authority&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set clear expectations, career paths,cross learning&amp;nbsp; and development plans for team members&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Foster a culture of ownership, accountability, learning, and innovation&lt;br&gt;Provide coaching and hands-on guidance while scaling team capability and maturity&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Stakeholder &amp;amp; Program Leadership&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as a trusted partner to senior Finance, Accounting, IT, and Business leaders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead cross-functional programs spanning multiple teams, vendors, and geographies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Balance competing priorities while maintaining delivery quality and stakeholder trust&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Twilio values diverse experiences from all kinds of industries, and we encourage everyone who meets the required qualifications to apply. If your career is just starting or hasn&#39;t followed a traditional path, don&#39;t let that stop you from considering Twilio. We are always looking for people who will bring something new to the table!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;15+ years of experience in Billings-to-Cash / Revenue systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven delivery of at least two (2) end-to-end implementations across Billing, AR, Revenue (ASC 606), and Cash processes, covering design, build, integration, go-live, and post-implementation stabilization&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep hands-on expertise in Zuora Billing and Zuora Revenue, including subscriptions, usage, pricing, amendments, invoicing, payments, and ASC 606 revenue recognition&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong hands-on experience with Oracle Cloud AR and Oracle Revenue Management, including invoicing, cash application, collections, accounting events, and revenue recognition&lt;br&gt;Strong understanding of CPQ → Billing → Revenue → ERP accounting flows across Zuora and Oracle ecosystems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven experience designing and governing complex, enterprise-scale integrations across SaaS platforms including Zuora, Oracle ERP, tax engines, payment gateways, banks, and usage mediation platforms&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Solid knowledge of financial close processes, including AR aging, reconciliations, revenue tie-outs, audit support, and SOX controls&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading large-scale programs, system implementations, transformations, and platform modernization initiatives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong people leadership skills with experience building, mentoring, and leading global teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent stakeholder management, communication, and problem-solving skills, with the ability to influence senior business and finance leadership&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working in Agile delivery models, including backlog management, releases, upgrades, and production support&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree in Engineering, Computer Science, Finance, or a related field (MBA preferred)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Desired:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Zuora Billing Solution Architect and/or Zuora Revenue Solution Architect certification&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oracle Financials Cloud certification (AR or Revenue preferred)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supporting high-volume, usage-based, or consumption billing models&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exposure to global billing, invoicing, localization, and tax compliance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supporting M&amp;amp;A integrations within Q2C platforms&lt;/li&gt;
