&lt;p&gt;At Webflow, we’re building the world’s leading AI-native Digital Experience Platform, and we’re doing it as a remote-first company built on trust, transparency, and a whole lot of creativity. This work takes grit, because we move fast, without ever sacrificing craft or quality. Our mission is to bring development superpowers to everyone. From entrepreneurs launching their first idea to global enterprises scaling their digital presence, we empower teams to design, launch, and optimize for the web without barriers. We believe the future of the web, and work, is more open, more creative, and more equitable. And we’re here to build it together.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are seeking an &lt;strong&gt;Partner Platforms Manager, AI &lt;/strong&gt;to design and own the systems orchestration layer that enables a scalable, reliable, and trusted partner ecosystem. This role focuses on connecting specialized tools and platforms—rather than building them from scratch—by defining how partner lifecycle state, eligibility, compliance, and decision logic are represented and automated across systems. The goal is to reduce operational friction, minimize financial risk, and ensure automation remains accurate, auditable, and resilient as complexity grows.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As partner programs mature, the challenge shifts from campaigns and tooling to building durable, cross-functional systems that integrate partners into go-to-market operations with clarity and correctness. In this role, you will translate complex business requirements into scalable, AI-assisted workflows that support onboarding, eligibility enforcement, routing, attribution, and financially sensitive processes. You will think deeply about APIs, data flows, and system boundaries to ensure external partners interact seamlessly with internal revenue, marketing, and finance systems.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will work closely with Partner Operations, Revenue Operations, and Marketing Operations, operating at the intersection of these teams while owning partner lifecycle logic and cross-system automation. This is a hands-on role — you will directly build, implement, and operate integrations and automation workflows, not solely advise on their design.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role is ideal for an engineer who enjoys designing connective infrastructure, thrives in multi-motion GTM environments such as agencies or partnerships, and is motivated by building systems that are not just functional, but trustworthy and future-proof.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the role:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;
