&lt;p&gt;As a &lt;strong&gt;Partner Platforms Manager, AI&lt;/strong&gt; you’ll…&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Design and own the partner systems orchestration layer:&lt;/strong&gt; Architect how partner-related systems work together across onboarding, enablement, deal collaboration, and incentives. You will define clear system boundaries, sources of truth, and integration patterns that keep partner data accurate and trustworthy&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Translate partner program requirements into system logic:&lt;/strong&gt; Convert complex partner rules and policies into deterministic, auditable workflows that govern partner eligibility, progression, and payout readiness. Ensure these rules scale without relying on manual review. You will think holistically about the partner lifecycle — from acquisition to onboarding, activation, and reporting — designing automation that reduces manual work while preserving financial and compliance safeguards.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Design automation with clear guardrails: &lt;/strong&gt;Build workflows that balance rule-based logic, AI-assisted decisioning, and human-in-the-loop checkpoints. You will be responsible for deciding where automation is appropriate and where correctness requires human oversight.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Apply AI selectively and responsibly: &lt;/strong&gt;Use AI to support triage, exception handling, and insight generation in partner operations. Establish evaluation and monitoring approaches to ensure automated outcomes remain explainable, accurate, and safe, especially in financially sensitive workflows.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Own cross-system integration and reliability: &lt;/strong&gt;Design and maintain integrations across PRM, partner management, enablement, and finance systems. Anticipate partial failures, asynchronous events, and data discrepancies, and design for reconciliation, recovery, and observability. You will work across lifecycle tooling including CRM data flows, partner enablement platforms, reporting systems, and workflow automation layers, ensuring partner lifecycle state is consistent and auditable across systems.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Ensure production readiness and operational clarity:&lt;/strong&gt; Define standards for monitoring, alerts, documentation, and runbooks for partner-critical systems. Make system behavior understandable and predictable for operational teams who rely on it day to day.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Partner closely across functions: &lt;/strong&gt;Collaborate with Partner Operations, Finance, RevOps, Marketing Operations, Support, and Engineering to ensure systems meet compliance, audit, and reliability expectations. Clearly communicate system behavior, constraints, and tradeoffs to both technical and non-technical stakeholders.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Design for change and long-term scalability:&lt;/strong&gt; Build systems that can evolve as partner programs change, minimizing technical debt and allowing underlying tools or vendors to be replaced without disrupting partner experience or business operations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About you:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;
