&lt;p&gt;As a &lt;strong&gt;Revenue Analytics Manager&lt;/strong&gt;, you’ll …&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own Customer Success and Partner analytics that drive retention, expansion, forecasting, and long term customer value&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Customer Success and Partners Leadership to deliver actionable insights, dashboards, and reporting that support account planning and prioritization&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Leverage AI tooling to speed up analysis, surface patterns across large datasets, and reduce time-to-insight for revenue stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help define where AI augments our workflows, from dashboard development to proactive risk and expansion signaling&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with Product and Data teams to connect product usage signals with customer outcomes and GTM motions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the development of customer health and expansion analytics, using product and GTM data to surface expansion opportunities and risk across existing accounts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own partnerships performance analytics and work alongside Partners Leadership to optimize sourced, influenced, and co sell motions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure data accuracy and consistency across Salesforce, Snowflake, and product analytics systems, maintaining a high bar for trust and usability&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate complex data into clear, compelling insights and recommendations for non-technical stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support ad hoc analytics requests across Customer Success, Partnerships, and broader GTM initiatives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About you:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Requirements:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5-7 years of experience in customer analytics, product analytics, or GTM analytics within a B2B SaaS environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree in Analytics, Business, Economics, Computer Science, or a related field, or equivalent practical experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong SQL skills and experience working with data warehouses such as Snowflake&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building dashboards and reporting in Tableau or comparable BI tools&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Solid understanding of post sales GTM motions including customer success, renewals, expansion, and partnerships&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with Salesforce and customer account data&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to translate data into clear, actionable insights for both individual contributors and leadership&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll thrive as a &lt;strong&gt;Revenue Analytics Manager&lt;/strong&gt; if you:&lt;/p&gt;
